    "summary": "A (tabby) cotton skirt cloth, a kain panjang, decorated in hand-drawn batik.  Hemmed at both short ends.  Background filling motif is gringsing against which are set vertical columns of larger motifs, alternating between columns made up of sections of a circle, almost a stylised lar, with concentric bands of patterning, and columns of more fragmentary motifs drawn from classical semen designs arranged neatly one above the other.  Finely glazed.  An accomplished piece of work.  [Text written by Dr Fiona Kerlogue, Horniman Museum.]",
